<title>UK: Abbot unit in Caspian Sea drill study.</title>
<headline>Abbot unit in Caspian Sea drill study.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Abbot Group said on Friday that its wholly-owned subsidiary KCA Drilling Ltd has been awarded a contract by Azerbaijan International Operating Company to execute a drilling study on three fields in the Caspian Sea.</p>
<p>Abbot said the study began on December 9, 1996 and is expected to take 12 weeks.</p>
<p>Abbot is conducting the study along with a unit of Canada's Dreco Energy Services Ltd for the next phase in the development of the Gunashli, Chirag and Azeri fields.</p>
<p>Azerbaijan International is a consortium of 11 international oil exploration groups.</p>
<p>The study is being done in Dreco Europe's London office with support from KCA's corporate office in Aberdeen and Dreco's corporate office in Edmonton.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
